# Work and trade between residents (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): chains. One asks after the other's work, or
# tells their own unasked; the other answers as their trade, their till, their purse and their temper make them; the
# first answers that in kind (work.reply, which reads how the news was told: pair.mem.w7_tone), and some close it
# (work.end). Bosses give orders (work.order) and hear pleas for pay or rest (work.plea).
#
# Tones a beat leaves for the reply (pair.mem.w7_tone, half an hour): low (bad news), high (good news), tired, busy,
# idle (slow but not ruinous), plain (nothing much).

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Asking after the work

rule w7_ask_trade
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=acquaintances|friends other.business=thriving|steady|failing pair.boss=no
cooldown 1d
say How's trade? | Selling much? | Shop keeping you? | Is the till singing or sulking? | Busy, are you?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_trade_close
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=friends|family|spouses other.business=thriving|steady|failing self.warmth=warm
cooldown 1d
say And the shop, #pet#? Truly, now. | How's the shop treating you, #pet#? | Tell me straight. How's business?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_rival
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=rivals other.business=thriving|steady|failing
cooldown 2d
say Still open, are you? | Heard your shelves were full. Nobody buying? | Keeping the doors open, I see. Just.
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_workmate
when concept=talk.work other.working=yes
cooldown 1d
say How's your end going? | You nearly done there? | Getting anywhere with it? | How's it looking your side?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_boss_checks
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=calm|even
cooldown 1d
say How are you getting on? | All going to plan? | Anything you need from me?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_boss_short
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=short|nervy
cooldown 1d
say Is it done yet? | Why's that not finished? | What have you been doing all morning?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_after_shift
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk|talk.day other.shift=after
cooldown 1d
say Long day? | Finished for the day, then? | How did the day go? | Knocked off at last?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_before_shift
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk other.shift=before
cooldown 1d
say Off to it, then? | Ready for the day? | What's waiting for you today?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_chatty
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk self.talk=chatty pair.band=acquaintances|friends other.working=yes
cooldown 2d
say Now then, what are you at? Tell me everything. | Ooh, what's that you're doing? Is it hard? | Don't let me stop you, but how's the work?
then other: work.answer

## Broad askings: almost anyone, to almost anyone (few criteria, many words)

rule w7_ask_any
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 1d
say How's the work? | Keeping busy? | Much on today? | How goes it? | Getting on all right?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_day
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=day
cooldown 1d
say Half the day gone already. How's yours? | Got much done? | What's the day thrown at you so far?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_dusk
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 1d
say Done for the day? | Was it a long one? | Getting home at last?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_dawn
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=dawn
cooldown 1d
say Up early as ever. Big day? | What's on for today? | You look half asleep. Long day ahead?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_friend
when concept=talk.work pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 1d
say How's it going, #pet#? Really. | Are they working you hard? | Tell me about your day.
then other: work.answer

## Same trade, asking shop talk

rule w7_ask_smith
when concept=talk.work self.job=smith other.job=smith pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say How's your iron behaving? | Fire drawing well your end? | Many orders in?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_baker
when concept=talk.work self.job=baker other.job=baker pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say Did your dough rise this morning? Mine sulked. | How's the oven? | What flour are you on now?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_farmer
when concept=talk.work self.job=farmer other.job=farmer pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say How's your ground? | Anything coming up your side? | How are the beasts?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_fisher
when concept=talk.work self.job=fisher other.job=fisher
cooldown 1d
say Fish biting for you? | Any luck this morning? | How were the nets?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_guard
when concept=talk.work self.role=guard other.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say Quiet on your beat? | Anything doing? | Trouble your way?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_healer
when concept=talk.work self.job=healer other.job=healer
cooldown 1d
say How are your patients? | Many in today? | Is the cough still going round your end?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_merchant
when concept=talk.work self.role=merchant other.role=merchant pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say Moving much? | How's the counting going? | Selling or just standing?
then other: work.answer

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Answering about the work (self answers)

rule w7_ans_plain
when concept=work.answer
say Steady. | Can't grumble. | Same as ever. | Ticking over. | Oh, you know. #work.capitalize#.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_short
when concept=work.answer temper=short
say Busy. Why? | It'd go faster without questions. | Fine. Is that all? | Don't ask.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merry
when concept=work.answer humour=merry
say Oh, wonderful. Nothing's caught fire since breakfast. | Grand! I've only cursed twice. | Splendid. Ask me again in an hour.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_dry
when concept=work.answer humour=dry
say Thrilling. I can hardly contain myself. | Much as yesterday. And the day before that. | It's #work#. It does what it does.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_guarded
when concept=work.answer honesty=guarded
say Well enough. | Can't say much. You know how it is. | It goes. | Why do you ask?
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_ambitious
when concept=work.answer drive=ambitious
say Well, and it'll be better. I've plans. | Good. Not good enough. Not yet. | Growing. You'll see.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_content
when concept=work.answer drive=content
say Suits me fine. Always has. | I've no complaints. The work's honest. | Same as my father had it. That's no bad thing.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_restless
when concept=work.answer drive=restless
say Same as ever. That's the trouble. | I could do this in my sleep. Some days I do. | Bored stiff, if you want the truth.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_quiet
when concept=work.answer talk=quiet
say Fine. | Mm. Good. | Going.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_chatty
when concept=work.answer talk=chatty
say Oh, where to start! First the cart was late, then the cart was early, then... | Busy, busy. Did I tell you about the new stool? It wobbles. | Good! Mostly. You'd not believe the morning I've had.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

## The till

rule w7_ans_steady
when concept=work.answer business=steady
say Steady. Pays the rent. | Not rich, not ruined. | Regulars keep me going. | Enough coming in, just.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_failing
when concept=work.answer business=failing
priority 1
say Badly. Nobody's buying. | Three days without a sale. Three. | I'll be shut by the month's end, the way it's going. | I count the till and it doesn't take long.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_thriving
when concept=work.answer business=thriving
priority 1
say Run off my paws! | Can't keep the shelves full. | Best month I've had. Touch wood. | Turning folk away, nearly.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_failing_proud
when concept=work.answer business=failing temper=short warmth=cold|reserved
priority 1
say Fine. It's fine. | Never better. | It'll pick up. It always picks up. | Mind your own till.
remember pair: w7_tone=proud 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_thriving_guarded
when concept=work.answer business=thriving honesty=guarded|sly
priority 1
say Oh, slow. Terribly slow. | Mustn't grumble. | Getting by, getting by.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_owes
when concept=work.answer owes=yes business=steady|failing
priority 1
say I'm working for the lender, not for me. | Everything I take goes out the door again. Debts. | I'd be fine if I didn't owe half the street.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_destitute
when concept=work.answer wealth=destitute
priority 2
say I'm working and still can't eat. Tell me how that's right. | There isn't enough work in the world to dig me out. | Every #money# is gone before I've earned it.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_tired
when concept=work.answer tired=yes working=yes
priority 1
say I'm asleep on my paws. | #tired.capitalize#. Ask me after I've slept. | Long. Very long. And not done yet. | I could lie down on this floor.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_tired_after
when concept=work.answer tired=yes shift=after
priority 1
say Done. Done in, too. | I've nothing left. Not a whisker. | Over. Thank the gods it's over.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_before
when concept=work.answer shift=before
say Not started. Don't remind me. | Off to it now. Wish me luck. | Ask me tonight.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_after
when concept=work.answer shift=after
say Done for the day, and glad of it. | Finished. Feet up soon. | It's behind me now. That's the best part.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_day_off
when concept=work.answer shift=day_off
say Not today! Day off. Don't spoil it. | I'm not thinking about it. Not one thought. | Ask me tomorrow. Today I'm a wolf of leisure.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_hurt
when concept=work.answer injured=light working=yes
priority 1
say Working one-pawed today. Took a knock. | Slower than usual. The arm. | Fine, if I don't lift anything. Which is the whole job.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

## The day's kind

rule w7_ans_market_merchant
when concept=work.answer here.day=market role=merchant
priority 1
say Market day! Don't ask me now. | Haven't sat since dawn. | Busy. It's market day. Everyone wants everything.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_market_food
when concept=work.answer here.day=market job=baker|cook|brewer|innkeeper
priority 1
say Market day. Cleared out by noon, I'll be. | Feeding half the county today. | Every stallholder wants feeding and every farmer wants a drink.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_restday
when concept=work.answer here.day=rest working=yes
priority 1
say Working Restday. Again. | Restday, they call it. Not for me. | Somebody has to.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_festival
when concept=work.answer here.day=festival working=yes
priority 1
say Working through the festival. Can you hear them out there? | Everyone's dancing but me. | Feast days are work days, for some of us.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

## The asker is the answerer's boss (work.answer comes second in a talk: the asker is a)

rule w7_ans_to_boss
when concept=work.answer pair.boss=a working=yes
say Getting there. | Nearly done, I promise. | On it. Right on it. | Going well. Honest.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_to_boss_tired
when concept=work.answer pair.boss=a working=yes tired=yes
priority 1
say Fine! Fine. Not tired at all. | Wide awake. Never better. *yawns* | Going well. Why, do I look tired?
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_to_boss_short
when concept=work.answer pair.boss=a working=yes temper=short
say It'll be done when it's done. | Faster if you'd stop asking. | I've two paws. Not four.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_to_boss_ambitious
when concept=work.answer pair.boss=a working=yes drive=ambitious
say Done, and I've started the next. | Finished early. Give me more. | Done. Have you thought about what I said? More hours?
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_apprentice
when concept=work.answer apprentice=yes
say Learning. Slowly. | I've ruined less than yesterday. | My master says I'm improving. Then sighs.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_master
when concept=work.answer master=yes
say Good, but the apprentice will be the death of me. | Teaching takes twice as long as doing. | Well. My pupil's coming on.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_house
when concept=work.answer self.house
say The House keeps us busy. Walls don't build themselves. | Steady. The House always has work. Pays when it pays. | Can't complain. It's House work. Regular.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_greatly
when concept=work.answer self.house=house_greatly working=yes
say Brick, lime, brick, lime. Greatly builds and I carry. | They're putting up another wall for House Greatly. My shoulders know. | Greatly's paint in my fur again. Never comes out.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fell
when concept=work.answer self.house=house_fell working=yes
say Sawdust in everything. House Fell's got orders stacked to the roof. | Planks, staves, wheels. Fell wants all of it yesterday. | Timber's wet. Fell says cut it anyway.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_grayrock
when concept=work.answer self.house=house_grayrock working=yes
say Grayrock's furnaces don't sleep. Nor do we, much. | Iron in, iron out. Grayrock counts every bar. | Hot, loud, and Grayrock's steward watching.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_mossgrave
when concept=work.answer self.house=house_mossgrave working=yes
say Dye to the elbows. Mossgrave blue, this week. | The tannery stinks and Mossgrave pays. That's the deal. | Wool, wool and more wool. Mossgrave's never short of sheep.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

## By trade (self answers)

rule w7_ans_smith
when concept=work.answer job=smith
say Iron's poor this month. Brittle. | Hinges, nails, hinges. Never a sword. | Burnt the same finger three times. Otherwise good.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker
when concept=work.answer job=baker
say Up since the third hour. | Dough sulked this morning, but it came round. | Flour in my ears, flour in my fur. Same as ever.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer
when concept=work.answer job=brewer
say The new batch is working. You can smell it from the street. | Barrels to scrub. Always barrels to scrub. | Good brew this time. Don't tell anyone.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_innkeeper
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper
say Full last night, and not one of them paid on time. | Rooms let, stools broken. A good week. | Quiet. Too quiet. The cellar's full and the room's empty.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_guard
when concept=work.answer role=guard
say Quiet. I like quiet. | Two drunks and a lost goat. | Boots wearing through. Otherwise fine.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_soldier
when concept=work.answer job=soldier
say Drill, polish, drill. | They march us up the hill and march us down again. | Waiting. Soldiering's mostly waiting.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer
when concept=work.answer job=farmer
say The ground's good, if the sky behaves. | Weeds grow faster than wages. | Beasts are fed. That's a day.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_spring
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=spring
priority 1
say Sowing. My back's in two pieces. | Seed's in. Now we wait and pray. | Ploughing till dark, every day.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_summer
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=summer
priority 1
say Haymaking. Every dry day counts. | Hoeing. Endless hoeing. | Watching the sky and the barley, both.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_autumn
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=autumn
priority 1
say Harvest. Don't talk to me till it's in. | Every paw in the field and still not enough. | Good yield this year. Or it will be, if the rain holds off.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_winter
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=winter
priority 1
say Mending fences and staring at the snow. | Winter. Nothing to do but feed the beasts and worry. | Sharpening everything I own, twice.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder
when concept=work.answer job=herder
say Flock's well. One wanders, but there's always one. | Counted them twice. Same number both times. | Ewes are fat and the dogs are lazy.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder_spring
when concept=work.answer job=herder here.season=spring
priority 1
say Lambing. I've not slept in a week. | Twins in the night, both living. | Up to my elbows in ewe. Don't shake my paw.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder_winter
when concept=work.answer job=herder here.season=winter
priority 1
say Hay's going faster than I'd like. | Brought them all down off the hill before the snow. | Breaking ice on the troughs every morning.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fisher
when concept=work.answer job=fisher
say Nets came up half full. Half empty, my wife says. | Fish are deep today. Sulking, like the rest of us. | Good catch. Smell my paws if you don't believe me.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fisher_storm
when concept=work.answer job=fisher here.weather=storm|fog
priority 1
say No boats out in this. Not mine, anyway. | Sat on the shore mending nets and watching the water. | The water's angry. I'll not argue with it.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_miner
when concept=work.answer job=miner
say Seam's thinning. | Dark and wet and the lamp keeps guttering. Normal, then. | Brought up good ore today. My back paid for it.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_healer
when concept=work.answer job=healer
say Coughs, cuts and one broken tail. | Busy. Everyone's ill at once, as usual. | Lost none today. That's a good day.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_healer_winter
when concept=work.answer job=healer here.season=winter
priority 1
say Coughs. Every chest in town is rattling. | Chilblains and fevers, door to door. | I've run out of willow bark twice this week.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_priest
when concept=work.answer job=priest
say The chapel's full on Restday and empty the rest. | Two weddings to plan and one burial. | The roof leaks on the altar. The gods are testing me.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_scholar
when concept=work.answer job=scholar
say I've read the same page eleven times. | Ink's run out and so has my patience. | I found an error in a book two hundred years old. Wonderful day.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_laborer
when concept=work.answer job=laborer
say Carried things from there to here. Tomorrow, from here to there. | Shoulders aching. Pay's coming, they say. | Work's work. It's #money#.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_carter
when concept=work.answer job=carter
say Road's rutted to the axle. | Mule's in a mood, I'm in a mood. | Two loads today and a wheel that squeals.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_crafter
when concept=work.answer job=crafter
say Three orders, and every one wanted yesterday. | Steady paws, steady work. | Spoiled a piece this morning. Started again.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_servant
when concept=work.answer job=servant
say The mistress has changed her mind about the curtains. Again. | Fetch, carry, polish, smile. | Silver's polished. The family's not.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_servant_heights
when concept=work.answer job=servant quarter=heights
priority 1
say Three dinners this week. Thirty guests. One of me. | They've guests from the other Houses. Everything has to shine. | The young master's back from the south. Heaven help us.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_cook
when concept=work.answer job=cook
say Burnt the onions, saved the stew. | The pot's been on since dawn. | Everyone wants feeding and nobody wants to pay.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_woodcutter
when concept=work.answer job=woodcutter
say Felled two and split one. | Axe needs grinding. So do I. | The wood's wet and so am I.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_official
when concept=work.answer job=official
say Paper. Mountains of it. | Three petitions, two complaints and a lost seal. | Every wolf in town wants a stamp on something.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_sailor
when concept=work.answer job=sailor
say Ashore till the cargo's loaded. Bored stiff. | Rigging to mend, decks to scrub. | Good wind coming. We'll be off soon.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_beggar
when concept=work.answer job=beggar
say Three pennies and a crust. Good day, for me. | Folk walk faster when they see me. | It's a trade like any other. Worse pay.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merchant
when concept=work.answer role=merchant
say Buying cheap, selling dear, or trying to. | The counting's the hard part. | Customers come in waves. Today's a dry tide.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_noble
when concept=work.answer job=noble
say Work? I sign things. Then I sign other things. | The steward does the work. I do the worrying. | Petitions, accounts, and a cousin who wants money.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_young
when concept=work.answer stage=young
say I fed the hens! All of them! | I carried a bucket all the way without spilling. Mostly. | I'm helping. Mum says I'm helping.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

## A trade and its till: the specific news

rule w7_ans_smith_failing
when concept=work.answer job=smith business=failing
priority 1
say Forge is cold half the day. No orders. | Nobody's mending anything. They're making do. | I've more hinges on the shelf than doors in town.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_smith_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=smith business=thriving
priority 1
say Orders till the month's end. Can't hammer fast enough. | Hinges, blades, shoes. The anvil hasn't been quiet in days. | Good iron and good custom. Mark the day.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker_failing
when concept=work.answer job=baker business=failing
priority 1
say Yesterday's loaves are today's loaves. And tomorrow's. | Baked forty, sold twelve. | They're buying from the other one. Cheaper, they say.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=baker business=thriving
priority 1
say Sold out by mid-morning. Every day this week. | They queue in the dark for my loaves now. | Another oven, that's what I need.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer_failing
when concept=work.answer job=brewer business=failing
priority 1
say Barrels full, purse empty. | The inns are buying elsewhere. | I'll be drinking my own stock at this rate. All of it.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=brewer business=thriving
priority 1
say Every barrel spoken for before it's tapped. | The town's thirsty and I'm the well. | Can't brew it fast enough. Lovely problem.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_inn_failing
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper business=failing
priority 1
say Empty rooms. Empty stools. Full cellar. | One guest all week, and he left without paying. | The fire's lit for nobody.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_inn_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper business=thriving
priority 1
say Every bed taken. I've had them sleeping on the benches. | Can't pour fast enough. | Full house every night. My feet hate me.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merchant_failing
when concept=work.answer role=merchant business=failing
priority 1
say Stock's gathering dust. I could sell the dust. | Folk look, folk touch, folk leave. | I've cut my prices to the bone and still nothing.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merchant_thriving
when concept=work.answer role=merchant business=thriving
priority 1
say Sold out of half the stock. Waiting on the carts. | Couldn't be better. Don't tell my rivals. | I'm thinking of a second stall.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_crafter_failing
when concept=work.answer job=crafter business=failing
priority 1
say Made it beautiful, and nobody wants beautiful. | No orders. I'm making things for the shelf now. | Folk mend their old ones instead.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_cook_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=cook|innkeeper business=thriving here.day=market|festival
priority 1
say The pot's emptied twice already. | Fed two hundred if I fed one. | Out of bread, out of stew, still they come.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Replying to what the other said of their work (self replies)

rule w7_rep_plain
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain
say Same as ever, then. | Aye, it goes. | Well, that's something. | #agree#. | That's #work# for you.

rule w7_rep_low
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low
say I'm sorry to hear it. | That's hard. | It'll turn. These things turn. | #oath#. That's no good.

rule w7_rep_high
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high
say Good for you. | Glad to hear it. | Long may it last. | Well! Somebody's doing well.

rule w7_rep_tired
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired
say Get some sleep. | You look it. | Go home. Lie down. | Don't fall asleep standing.

rule w7_rep_busy
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy
say I'll let you get on. | Don't let me keep you. | Better busy than idle. | Rather you than me.

rule w7_rep_idle
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=idle
say It'll come. | Quiet days are rest days. | Enjoy it while it lasts. | Put your feet up, then.

rule w7_rep_proud
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=proud
say If you say so. | That's not what I heard. | Course it is. | Right you are.

rule w7_rep_proud_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=proud warmth=warm pair.band=friends|family|spouses
say You can tell me, you know. I'll not tell a soul. | #pet.capitalize#. I've seen the shelves. | Say it as it is. It's only me.
then other: work.end

## Bad news, answered as the replier is

rule w7_rep_low_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low warmth=warm
say If it comes to it, you come to me first. You hear? | Oh, #pet#. It'll turn. I'll send folk your way. | Don't carry it alone. Come by tonight.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_cold
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low warmth=cold
say Hm. Well, that's trade. | Some do, some don't. | Then work harder.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_rival
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low pair.band=rivals
say Is it? Shame. | Oh dear. Oh dear, oh dear. | I'd offer to help, but you'd only refuse.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_thriving
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low business=thriving
say Mine's doing well, if that helps. It doesn't, does it. | Odd. My till's never been fuller. | Funny, I can't keep up. Want my overflow?

rule w7_rep_low_failing
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low business=failing
say Mine too. It's the whole town. | You and me both. Nobody's spending. | Don't. I could have said the same word for word.

rule w7_rep_low_poor
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low wealth=poor|destitute
say Join the club. Plenty of room. | We're all scraping, #address#. | Welcome to my life.

rule w7_rep_low_rich
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low wealth=rich warmth=warm
say If it's a matter of #money#, come and see me. Quietly. | I could put something your way. No, I mean it. | Let me buy a few things. It's no charity, I need them.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_devout
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low piety=devout
say I'll say a word for you on Restday. | The gods see honest work. They do. | Light a candle. It can't hurt.

rule w7_rep_low_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low humour=dry
say Could be worse. You could be me. | Well, the rats will be pleased. | At least it's quiet.

rule w7_rep_low_merry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low humour=merry
say Chin up! Worse things happen at sea. I've seen them. | Come on, I'll buy you a cup. A small one. | You'll laugh about it in a year. I'll laugh now, to save time.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_ambitious
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low drive=ambitious
say Then change something. Sell something else. | Move the stall. Lower the price. Shout louder. | Sitting still is how shops die.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low pair.boss=b
say Does that mean... are my wages safe? | Should I be looking for other work? | We'll pull through. Won't we?
then other: work.plea

rule w7_rep_low_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low stage=old
say I've seen worse years. You'll come through. | It was the same when I was your age. It passed. | Lean years and fat years. Hold on.

## Good news, answered as the replier is

rule w7_rep_high_poor
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high wealth=poor|destitute
say Must be nice. | Good for some. | Spare a thought for the rest of us.

rule w7_rep_high_failing
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high business=failing
say While mine starves. Lovely. | Glad someone's selling. | Teach me, then. Go on.

rule w7_rep_high_rival
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high pair.band=rivals
say Luck. It won't last. | Funny. I heard different. | Enjoy it. Fashions change.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_high_sly
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high honesty=sly
say Then you can buy the ale. | Lend us a penny, then. | Remember your friends, eh? Me, specifically.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_high_ambitious
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high drive=ambitious
say Tell me how. I mean it. | What's the secret? Prices? The spot? | Lucky. I'll make my own.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_high_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high warmth=warm
say Oh, that's lovely. You've earned it. | That does my heart good. | Didn't I tell you it'd come right?

rule w7_rep_high_devout
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high piety=devout
say Thank the gods for it. And tithe, mind. | Blessings come to honest paws. | Don't forget the chapel box.

rule w7_rep_high_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high pair.boss=b
say Then a little extra in my #wages# wouldn't hurt? | Good. So you'll be wanting more help? | And who sold most of it, I wonder?
then other: work.plea

## Tired, busy, idle: answered as the replier is

rule w7_rep_tired_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired stage=old
say Wait till you're my age. | You're young. You'll bounce. | I remember being that tired. Now I'm just old.

rule w7_rep_tired_tired
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired tired=yes
say You and me both. | Don't talk to me about tired. | We'll sleep standing, like horses.

rule w7_rep_tired_merry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired humour=merry
say Sleep's for the rich and the dead. | I'll prop you up with a broom. | Go and lie in the cart. Nobody'll notice.

rule w7_rep_tired_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired warmth=warm pair.boss=no
say Sit. Just for a moment. I'll not tell. | Here, lean on the wall. | Go to #bed# early tonight. Promise me.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_tired_boss_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired pair.boss=a warmth=warm
say Then finish that and get home. I'll manage. | Go on, knock off early. Just today. | Sit down a moment. The work will wait.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_tired_boss_cold
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired pair.boss=a warmth=cold|reserved
say Tired? There's an hour yet. | I don't pay you to yawn. | Sleep on your own time.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_busy_merchant
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy role=merchant
say Lucky. My side's dead. | Send the overflow my way. | Same here. Don't stop to talk.

rule w7_rep_busy_failing
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy business=failing
priority 1
say Busy? Mine's dead as a doornail. | Send a few my way. Please. | I'd give a paw for busy.

rule w7_rep_busy_rival
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy pair.band=rivals
priority 1
say Busy losing money, I expect. | Enjoy it. They'll be back with me by Restday. | Folk try everything once.

rule w7_rep_busy_idle_self
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy shift=day_off|after
say And here's me with my feet up. Sorry. | I'd help, but I'm enjoying watching. | Busy's good. Busy pays.

rule w7_rep_idle_restless
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=idle drive=restless
say Quiet's worse than busy. I'd go mad. | I'd be climbing the walls. | Then do something else. I would.

rule w7_rep_plain_chatty
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain talk=chatty
say Oh, I know just what you mean. Mine's the same. Let me tell you... | Isn't it always! My cousin says the same. | Same here, same here. Did you hear about the miller?

rule w7_rep_plain_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain humour=dry
say Thrilling news. | Stop, I can't take the excitement. | I'll write it in my book of wonders.

rule w7_rep_plain_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain pair.boss=a
say Good. Keep at it. | Right. Shout if you need me. | Mind you do it properly.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_plain_young
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain stage=young
say When I'm big I'm going to do that too. | Can I help? I'm good at helping. | Is it hard? It looks hard.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Closing (self speaks the last word)

rule w7_end_plain
when concept=work.end
say Aye. Well. | Right. | Back to it, then. | #saying#. | We'll see.

rule w7_end_working
when concept=work.end working=yes shift=during
say Right. Back to it. | Better get on. | This won't do itself. | I'll get on, then.

rule w7_end_thanks_warm
when concept=work.end warmth=warm
say #thanks#. Really. | You're good to me. | I'll remember that.

rule w7_end_short
when concept=work.end temper=short
say Hmph. | We'll see. | If you say so.

rule w7_end_merry
when concept=work.end humour=merry
say Ha! Go on with you. | You're a tonic, you are. | I'll hold you to that, mind.

rule w7_end_tired
when concept=work.end tired=yes
say Mm. Bed. Soon. | If I live that long. | Yes. Right. *yawns*

rule w7_end_proud
when concept=work.end business=failing honesty=guarded|frank warmth=cold|reserved
say I don't need help. I'll manage. | It'll come right on its own. | Keep your pity.

rule w7_end_dusk
when concept=work.end here.time=dusk shift=during|after
say Nearly lamp-lighting. Nearly home. | Not long now. | One more hour. One.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Telling, unasked (self opens with their own news)

rule w7_tell_failing
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=failing pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 12h
say I've to tell someone. The shop's going under. | I counted the till twice this morning. It didn't help. | If nothing changes, I'm shut by the month's end.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_thriving
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=thriving pair.band=friends|family|spouses|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say Sold out again. Third day running. | I've had to turn folk away. Turn them away! | Best week the shop's ever had.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_boast_rival
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=thriving pair.band=rivals
cooldown 2d
say Queue outside my door again this morning. Did you see? | Funny how folk know quality when they taste it. | I may have to hire. Business is that good.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_tired
when concept=talk.work tired=yes working=yes
cooldown 1d
say I could sleep on this bench. | If I sit down, I'll not get up. | My eyes keep closing on their own.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_restday
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.day=rest working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Restday, and here we are. | Everyone at chapel but us. | I'll rest when I'm dead, apparently.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_market_rush
when concept=talk.work here.day=market role=merchant other.role=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Market day and I've three paws too few. | I've sold more by noon than all last week. | Who are all these folk? Where do they come from?
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_owes
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk owes=yes pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 12h
say Every #money# I make goes to the lender. Every one. | I owe more than the shop's worth. Don't tell anyone. | I lie awake doing sums.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_apprentice_grumble
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk apprentice=yes pair.boss=no
cooldown 1d
say My master had me sweep the yard three times. Three. | Five years of this before I'm my own wolf. | I've learnt more from watching than from being told.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_master_grumble
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk master=yes pair.band!=apprentice
cooldown 1d
say My apprentice dropped a whole tray. A whole tray. | I was that clumsy once. I'm sure I wasn't. | Teaching's harder than the trade.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_ambitious
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk drive=ambitious business=thriving|steady pair.band=friends|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say I'm going to buy the shop next door. You watch. | One stall's a living. Two's a business. | Five years from now, my name over a proper door.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_restless
when concept=talk.work drive=restless working=yes
cooldown 2d
say I've done this same thing every day for six years. | Do you ever think of just walking out the gate? | One day I'll leave all this and go to sea.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_content
when concept=talk.work drive=content working=yes
cooldown 2d
say Good honest work, this. I'd not swap it. | My father did this, and his. Suits me. | There's a rhythm to it. I like the rhythm.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_poor_wages
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk wealth=poor|destitute working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Worked all week and I've four pennies to show. | The #wages# don't cover the rent. Not near. | Working and still hungry. How's that right?
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_old_hands
when concept=talk.work stage=old working=yes
cooldown 2d
say My paws aren't what they were. The work's the same. | Forty years at this. My knees know every one. | The young ones do it faster. Not better. Faster.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_young_hand
when concept=talk.work stage=adolescent working=yes other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Is it always this hard? | They gave me the worst job again. Because I'm new. | I did it right first time today! Nobody saw.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_hurt
when concept=talk.work injured=light working=yes
cooldown 12h
say Caught my paw in it this morning. Still throbbing. | Working with a #hurt# shoulder. Don't laugh. | Pulled something lifting. Pulled everything, maybe.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_dusk
when concept=talk.work here.time=dusk working=yes shift=during
cooldown 1d
say Light's going. Can't see what I'm doing. | Almost lamp-lighting. Almost free. | Another hour and I'm done. One more.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_dawn
when concept=talk.work here.time=dawn working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Too early for this. Far too early. | Sun's not up and nor am I, properly. | First one in again. Nobody else wants dawn.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_rain_outdoor
when concept=talk.work here.weather=rain|storm job=farmer|laborer|woodcutter|herder|carter|fisher
cooldown 1d
say Soaked to the skin and the work's not half done. | My fur's never going to dry. | This #rain# gets in everywhere. Everywhere.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_snow_outdoor
when concept=talk.work here.weather=snow job=farmer|laborer|woodcutter|herder|carter|guard
cooldown 1d
say Can't feel my paws. | Snow in my boots, snow in my ears. | Everything takes twice as long in this.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_heat_forge
when concept=talk.work here.season=summer here.weather=clear job=smith|baker|cook|brewer
cooldown 1d
say Summer and a fire all day. I'm cooked. | My tongue's out like a dog's. | Who wants hot work in this? Me, apparently.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_comfortable_steady
when concept=talk.work business=steady pair.band=friends|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say Steady week. I'll take steady. | Nothing grand, nothing awful. Paid the rent. | Regulars came, regulars paid. That's a good week.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_rich_bored
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk wealth=rich business=thriving|steady
cooldown 2d
say Honestly, I could stop. I just don't know what I'd do. | The ledgers keep me busier than the trade now. | I've hired another pair of paws. Strange, being the one who pays.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

## Broad tellings: almost anyone (few criteria)

rule w7_tell_any_plain
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 1d
say Same old, same old. | Another day, another #money#. Well, half a one. | I swear the work grows when I'm not looking. | Thought I'd finish early. Thought wrong.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_good_day
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 2d
say Good day today. Everything went right, for once. | Do you know, I think I did good work today. | Not one thing broke. Not one. I'm suspicious.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_bad_day
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 2d
say Everything I touched today went wrong. | One of those days. You know the sort. | If the morning's anything to go by, I should go home now.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_tools
when concept=talk.work stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Broke my best tool this morning. Twenty years I had it. | Someone's moved my things again. Nobody admits it. | New tool. Stiff as a board. It'll learn.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_customer
when concept=talk.work stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Had a customer today who wanted it cheaper, quicker and better. Pick two, I said. | Somebody paid me in buttons. Buttons! | A pup came in and asked if I was rich. I laughed for an hour.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_weekend
when concept=talk.work here.day=work
cooldown 2d
say How many days to Restday? Don't tell me. I'll cry. | I'm counting the hours to Restday. | Restday can't come soon enough.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- The boss and the worker

rule w7_boss_order
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=calm|even
cooldown 1d
say When you're done there, the yard wants sweeping. | Leave that. I need you on the front today. | Take your time with it. Do it right.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_short
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=short|nervy
cooldown 1d
say Faster. We're behind. | Not like that. Like I showed you. | I said before noon. It's past noon.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_market
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a here.day=market self.role=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Market day. Smile at everyone. Even the ones who don't buy. | Watch the front. Watch the pockets. | Stack them high. Folk buy what looks plenty.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_failing
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.business=failing
cooldown 1d
say Mind the waste. Every scrap counts now. | We'll have to tighten belts a while. | Don't light the second lamp. We can't spare it.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_boss_order_thriving
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.business=thriving self.warmth=warm|reserved
cooldown 2d
say Good work this week. I mean that. | We're doing well. You've helped. | Keep this up and we'll talk about your #wages#.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_praise_warm
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.warmth=warm other.working=yes
cooldown 2d
say That's good work. Neat. | You've a knack for that. | I'd not have done it better myself.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_scold_cold
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.warmth=cold other.tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say You're dragging your tail. | Are you working or dreaming? | If you're tired, there's others who'd want your place.
then other: work.order

rule w7_worker_asks_wage
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say Any chance of my #wages# early? Just this once. | The rent's due. Could you pay me a few days ahead? | Could I have what I've earned so far?
then other: work.plea

rule w7_worker_asks_raise
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b self.drive=ambitious
cooldown 3d
say I've been here long enough to earn a bit more. | I do the work of two. Pay me for one and a half? | Others pay better, you know. I've stayed.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_worker_asks_rest
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b self.tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say Could I have the afternoon? I'm dead on my paws. | Can I sit a moment? Just a moment. | Can I go home early? I'll come in at dawn.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_worker_asks_festival
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b world.festival=soon
cooldown 2d
say Can I have the festival day? My family's expecting me. | Will we shut for the festival? | I'd work the festival if you paid double.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_worker_asks_late_pay
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b other.business=failing
cooldown 1d
say I've not been paid this week. | Will there be #wages# on Restday? | Folk are saying the shop's in trouble. Is it?
then other: work.plea

## The worker answers an order (self is the worker, or whoever was asked)

rule w7_ord_plain
when concept=work.order
say Right away. | Aye. On it. | I'll see to it. | Yes, all right.

rule w7_ord_short
when concept=work.order temper=short
say I'm doing it. | Yes, yes. | I heard you the first time.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_tired
when concept=work.order tired=yes
say Yes. Right. In a moment. | If my legs agree. | ...Yes. Sorry. Yes.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_merry
when concept=work.order humour=merry
say At once, your lordship! | Your wish, my command. My aching command. | I'll sweep it so clean you can eat off it. Don't, though.

rule w7_ord_ambitious
when concept=work.order drive=ambitious
say Done by noon. And then what? | Leave it with me. And the rest, if you like. | I'll do it. Then can I try the hard work?

rule w7_ord_sly
when concept=work.order honesty=sly
say Of course. Who'd notice if I took a little longer? | Yes, yes. Will you be watching? | Right away. More or less.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_apprentice
when concept=work.order apprentice=yes
say Yes, master. | Like this? Is this right? | I'll get it right this time. I will.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_young
when concept=work.order stage=adolescent
say Why do I always get the sweeping? | Fine. But I'm doing the good bit after. | Can't someone else? ...Fine.

rule w7_ord_praised
when concept=work.order warmth=warm|reserved drive=steady|ambitious pair.boss=a
say Thank you. That means something. | I've been trying. | I'll keep it up.

## The boss answers a plea (self is the boss, or the one asked)

rule w7_plea_plain
when concept=work.plea
say We'll see. | Let me think on it. | Not today. Ask me again. | Perhaps.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_warm
when concept=work.plea warmth=warm
say Go on, then. Just this once. | Of course. You've earned it. | I'll do what I can. I promise.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_cold
when concept=work.plea warmth=cold
say No. | You'll get what you're owed when it's owed. | If you don't like it, there's the door.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_failing
when concept=work.plea business=failing
priority 1
say There's nothing to give. I'm sorry. Truly. | I'm paying you before I pay myself, as it is. | If it picks up. If.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_thriving_warm
when concept=work.plea business=thriving warmth=warm|reserved
priority 1
say Fair's fair. A bit more from next week. | Business is good. You'll see some of it. | I'll not forget who carried the load.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_thriving_cold
when concept=work.plea business=thriving warmth=cold
priority 1
say Good trade is my reward for my risk. Not yours. | We'll see how the month ends. | You're paid what we agreed.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_short
when concept=work.plea temper=short
say Don't push your luck. | Ask me again and I'll halve it. | Back to work.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_sly
when concept=work.plea honesty=sly
say Course. Next week. Definitely next week. | Remind me Restday. I'll have forgotten, mind. | Leave it with me. I'll see what I can see.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_rich
when concept=work.plea wealth=rich warmth!=cold
say Here. Don't make a habit of it. | Fine. I can spare it. | Go on. I'll not miss it.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_poor_boss
when concept=work.plea wealth=poor|destitute
say With what? I've less than you. | I'd pay you if I could pay me. | Look in the till. Go on, look.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_devout_restday
when concept=work.plea piety=devout here.day=rest
say It's Restday. Go. Go home. I shouldn't have kept you. | Go to chapel. The work can wait for the gods. | Of course. Rest. It's what the day's for.
then other: work.end
